<h1>Gettin’ a Granddaddy Lobster</h1><br/><br/><strong>
A smidgen out away from where the sea grasses swoon and sway<br/>
In the pitted limestone rock floor of the beautiful Florida Bay<br/>
Lives a large, grand fatherly, spiny lobster hidden in a cavernous hole<br/>
Just praying not to be tickled out by someone’s long, slender pole!<br/>
His sneaky antennae stick out like two pieces of black, dead grass<br/>
To the unsuspecting eyes who see no hint of the good eatin’ hind mass<br/>
That lies concealed in the shadows beneath a rocky crevice with a crack.<br/>
But to the experienced ones who know what they’re lookin’ at, their lips smack <br/>
And a rush of excitement blows through their snorkel tube and bubbles out<br/>
As they lure that Lobster into their net and swiftly surface to scream and shout!<br/>
